  "root_review": "Read complete4383-byte Latin target projection,4386-byte continuous old Mame comparison and4804-byte existing English, all declared lexical/pointing/cross differences, complete new Latin proof and final notes, plus independent whole-unit findings and both exact metadata successors. Rehashed six new source files and their dependencies, parsed source TOMLs, verified current exact proper/Latinproof/Englishbinding preimages,379-byte preserved prefix, unchanged English and frame. Source-page image collation is attributed to the independent reviewer; Root did not newly rasterize/view these source pages.",
  "whole_expression_publication_judgment": "Accept the exact underlying Latin prayer words from continuous Mame1922 unit AP368–378/printed254–264 under its registered United States public-domain textual basis. Every lexical word is independently old; target pointing/case/sign placements and foecund-to-fecund spelling are declared non-expressive editorial transformations. This is a bounded historical-source projection, not a blanket1962 or restored-Holy-Week grant and not a collection of scattered phrases.",
  "metadata_disposition": "Correct the predecessor Pustet Adesto/Respice ending misattribution and false English full-coverage language. V4 adds only two missing periods. V5 distinguishes actual separately stored n997/998 entries from complete ritual assembly; source existence is not performance completeness. All earlier source artifacts and frozen receipts remain intact.",
  "limits": [
    "Printed prayer text once only; Descendat repetitions, initial greeting/Oremus, rubrics/gestures/ministers, font branches and later units are not supplied by this body.",
    "Historical English remains an unchanged incomplete excerpt with omitted dialogue, abbreviated conclusions and literal word by fire. Full clean English execution remains separately required.",
    "No finite Latin authority expansion or existing f79/b26 ending rebind is implied; explicit positive-source epoch transition and current semantic merge are required.",
    "Guarded driver separately reviewed before preparation/integration. Root-exclusive canonical install uses exact fresh preimages; no stale full-owner replacement.",
    "Final actual source/consumer/public-surface gates required; no whole Vigil completion claim."
